{
  "id": "bigville_farm",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "depends_on": [],
  "self_load_only": true,
  "description": "bigville R52 (block 368000): REAL FARMS -- on the map, worked by farmhands, with livestock that live and die. A Farm (a Place{kind:farm} on the map's outskirts) has FIELDS and ANIMALS. fm_harvest: a ripe field is reaped by the FARMHANDS who work it (worker -works-> farm; yield = area*fertility*min(1, hands*per_worker)*town.weather_factor) -- no hands, no harvest (the crop rots); understaffed -> partial; the weather_factor is the HOOK the real weather system drives (a good season -> a bumper crop, a poor one -> a lean harvest). Cropping DEPLETES the soil. fm_fertilize closes the nutrient loop (manure/night-soil -> fertility). LIVESTOCK LIVE AND DIE: fa_grow (age + weight each season, drop manure), fa_breed (a mature dam+sire -> a calf, the herd grows), fa_die_oldage (past its lifespan -> a carcass), fa_slaughter (killed -> MEAT). So the farm is a living place worked by people. Composes with the map (the farm is a Place), bigville_office (a farmhand is a hired role), bigville_weather (drives weather_factor + affects the herd), bigville_waste (night-soil = fertilizer), and bigville_foodstuff (grain + meat = food).",
  "nodes": [],
  "edges": [],
  "productions": [],
  "concepts": [],
  "rules": [
    {
      "name": "fm_harvest",
      "batch": false,
      "comment": "A RIPE field is reaped by the FARMHANDS who work it (yield = area*fertility*min(1,hands*per_worker)*WEATHER): no hands -> the crop rots; understaffed -> partial; a drought year (low weather_factor) -> a poor harvest, a good year -> a bumper crop. Cropping depletes the soil; the field is reset (sown=0, ripe=0). LIGHT: only workers who can SEE count -- a worker who sees_dark (an outdoor field on a moonless/overcast night) cannot reap. sees_dark defaults 0 (can see), so a field by DAY or by MOONLIGHT is reaped in full; a dark night yields nothing. Composes with bigville_daynight.",
